<decision #track.replace_operations_with_actions.scope {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = false
  confidence = 0.99
  reversibility = "moderate"
}
(
  <question ?>How is terminology migrated?</?>
  <recommendation ?>Use action across the release surface and retain legacy terms only in migration boundaries.</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>operations → actions 应当连文件、字符串、配置和运行时术语一起彻底改；增加 std/commands。</?>
    <decision-text ?>Use action everywhere in the product surface; operation remains only in explicit compatibility, migration, fixture, and historical boundaries.</?>
    <rationale ?>The current interface has one vocabulary while upgrade-workspace owns the supported migration path.</?>
    <evidence ?>Accepted Mission decision `mission.evolve_codument_action_system.action_taxonomy`.</?>
  )
  >
)
>
